  "publication_notes": [
    "The first workflow-publication orchestration failed JavaScript parsing because a YAML expression collided with a JavaScript template expression. No mutation executed in that failed call. The workflow string encoding was corrected before publication.",
    "Actual CI run39670837599 failed workflow validation before any job: runner.temp is not permitted in job-level env. Use the owned relative Cargo target directory instead. No compiler/test execution occurred in this failed run.",
    "Actual run39670971206 installed official Rust1.90 and fetched the locked dependencies, then refused before compiler launch because the original guard's fixed cgroup-v2 memory.current path was absent. Artifact12380255676 SHA256fc79a68b71e585eafb11739d35caab4dac389e78613a8f06c6bd8a5330295100 retains the error receipt. The NEW owned adapter reuses the exact original supervisor/limits and permits only a validated mounted cgroup-v1 memory root counter; no unbounded fallback or old held-job replay.",
    "Actual run39671217634 also refused before compiler launch: neither fixed root counter was available. Linux cgroup-v2 documentation confirms memory.current is a NON-ROOT cgroup file. Successor adapter resolves the actual /proc/self/cgroup membership against the actual cgroup mount root, rather than guessing the global root location; rejects path escapes/missing counters. It retains the original supervisor and thresholds and names the actual counter scope.",
    "Run39671453994 actually compiled Rust with the retained lock and validated cgroup-v2 current membership; original8 groups passed,4 new groups panicked on a usize intermediate subtraction in polynomial division. One arithmetic-index expression is corrected from top-d.len()+1 to top+1-d.len(); fresh tests required. Full failure/correction record is retained.",
    "Run39672776803 passed the original/native and NEW actual codec CLI + original facade controls. MCP-only harness failed before protocol because -I suppresses server.py's required sibling bridge import. Correct only the harness argv to -E -s -B; original server/bridge/runtime remain unchanged. Fresh MCP execution required.",
